=begin
      author: Fizzleworth
        name: infuse
        game: gemstone
        tags: scroll infusion, infuse, unlock, runestone, scroll
    requires: Lich > 5.4.0
     version: 2.2
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).


Infuse!
	
    This script will automatically unlock and infuse scrolls for you! 

	The script always uses the quiss'fyn rune to unlock. By default it unlocks every
	locked spell on the scroll; with --spells=<n,n> it unlocks only until the spells you
	list are unlocked (see below) and ignores the rest.
	
    You must first define your infuse and scroll sack (which can be the same):

		;vars set infusesack=<container name>
        # for runestones and runestone-making tools (brush, ink, cup)
        ;vars set scrollsack=<container name>
        # for finished scrolls

    Optionally, define a separate sack for vibrant-ink scrolls (those whose
    spell descriptions come back "vibrant" when checked). If unset, vibrant
    scrolls are stored in scrollsack along with everything else.

        ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=<container name>
        # for finished vibrant-ink scrolls

    Optionally, turn off the safety pause. By default (infuse_safe=true), if an
    infusion is a struggle ("You strain to harness the mana...") the script stops
    and waits 10 seconds for you to NOD before it keeps going, and gives up if you
    don't. With infuse_safe=false it skips that check and keeps trying.

        ;vars set infuse_safe=false

	Other assumptions:
		- You have at least 20,000 silvers in your local bank (withdrawn as a flat
		  amount whenever a rune needs to be made, to cover runestones/ink/cup/etc.)
		- Ideally you have backroom access to the general store: a blank runestone is
		  then made for about 6k instead of 10k by buying a "smooth stone" there and an
		  aish'vrak potion from the alchemist, and pouring one on the other (the stone
		  is still a runestone for rummage purposes, just with the noun "stone"). With
		  no backroom access it buys the alchemist's premade runestone instead, and
		  ;vars set infuse_smooth_stone=false skips the extra general store stop.
		- You can read all scrolls
		- If you die (a scroll can kill you outright), the script stops itself at once
		  instead of carrying on with a dead character
		- You're not carrying a heavy load of silvers: if your encumbrance is 25% or more
		  and you have silvers on hand, the script runs to the bank, deposits them all and
		  comes back before doing anything else (change the 25 with
		  ;vars set infuse_max_encumbrance=<percent>, or 0 to turn it off)
		- Closed containers are fine: infusesack, scrollsack, vibrantscrollsack and any
		  --cont container are opened as needed and closed again afterward (only the
		  ones the script opened - anything already open is left open)
	
    Once you have the variables set, you can activate the script in the following ways:
	
		;infuse
			- Unlock (all locked spells, or just the --spells ones) & infuse the scroll in your right hand
	
		;infuse unlock 
			- Unlock the scroll in your right hand: every locked spell, or only until the
			  --spells ones are unlocked
		
		;infuse infuse
			- Fully infuse an unlocked scroll in your right hand. This does not check whether the scroll has been unlocked.
    
		;infuse rune <rune name>
			- Creates the rune of your choice

		;infuse check
			- Check the charges/unlock status of the scroll in your right hand, then
			  stow it in scrollsack (or vibrantscrollsack)

		;infuse help
			- Show usage and your current settings

	Any of the above (unlock-only and rune excepted, since they stow nothing) also
	takes --cont=<container>, which puts the finished scroll in that container
	instead of scrollsack/vibrantscrollsack - handy for scrolls you're passing
	along to another character, e.g.:

		;infuse --cont=kit

	--spells=<n,n> limits unlocking to the spells you care about. quiss'fyn
	unlocks a random locked spell each wave and only unlocked spells get
	infused, so with this the script waves quiss'fyn, checks with odeir'cos, and
	repeats until every listed spell is unlocked (ignoring the rest), then goes
	on to link and infuse. It won't wave at all if a listed spell isn't on the
	scroll, and it stops if the scroll can't be unlocked any further while a
	listed spell is still locked. Works with unlock and the default command:

		;infuse --spells=101,103

    NotAramund's note:        
	I adapted Ashraam's infuse.lic to create this script. I had the following goals in mind:
		- Create a no-fuss way to fully unlock scrolls for my Thaumaturgy Tome
		- Separate out the pieces of that process in case someone needs them individually
		
    Fizzleworth's note:    
	I updated Ashraam's and NotAramund's script with the following fixes:
        - Fixed palimpsests not working
        - Fixed runestone making not working
        - Put finished scroll in a scrollsack (set with ;vars)
        - Removed "infuse_scroll" and replaced with "infuse"
        - Stop cleanly if too injured to cast the link spell (714) instead of hanging
        - Detect when the link to the scroll slips mid-infuse and relink automatically
        - Store finished vibrant-ink scrolls in a separate vibrantscrollsack (set with ;vars)
        - ;infuse help now shows current settings and what each sack is for
        - Widened several 1-second response timeouts to 5 seconds; on a slow connection
          they could time out before the game's reply arrived, causing false
          "not enough money" / "something went wrong" errors and a stuck rune-unlock loop
        - Unlocking now checks with odeir'cos first to see how many spells are still
          locked, then waves quiss'fyn exactly that many times instead of waving blindly
          until the scroll reports fully unlocked
        - Fixed infuse getting stuck repeatedly failing after the ag'loenar runestone
          shatters: the response's terminator regex didn't include that phrase, so it
          never reached the code that already existed to fetch a new one
        - Fixed unlocking never stopping (kept waving after the scroll was already
          fully unlocked, burning runes/mana): the "altered" success check hardcoded
          the word "scroll", but the game substitutes the item's real noun (e.g.
          "vellum"), so the locked-count never decremented on non-scroll items. Also
          added a safety net that stops if the game itself reports nothing left to
          unlock, regardless of what the count says.
        - That safety net only matched one exact "nothing left to unlock" phrasing
          ("shakes violently, but nothing happens"), missing other flavor-text
          variants ("shakes slightly, but nothing happens", "is momentarily
          surrounded by a dim white aura") and wasting several waves before the
          disintegrate check finally caught it. Broadened to match loosely instead
          of one hardcoded phrasing.
        - Fixed rune-making failing at Sorena's (Icemule): the ink there is sold as
          "a ... ink bottle" (noun "bottle"), so "dip brush in my ink" silently
          no-opped and the draw errored out with "Something went wrong". The dip and
          put-away now read the ink item's real noun off the item in hand instead
          of assuming "ink", and a leftover ink bottle is reused instead of
          re-ordered.
        - Fixed rune-making stowing the rune brush: with a hand already full, "get cup"
          failed and the blind "stow left" retry stowed the brush instead, so the dip
          and draw silently failed. Hands are now cleared up front, and the
          free-a-hand retry skips the brush. Whatever was in your hands is
          remembered, stowed with "stow all", and picked back up afterward.
        - Added the infuse_safe setting (default true). When a struggling infusion asks
          you to nod, true keeps the old pause-and-confirm; false skips it and keeps
          trying (;vars set infuse_safe=false).
        - Fixed a fully-unlockable scroll being reported "locked" mid-infuse: "You are not
          prepared to infuse that" also happens when the link to the scroll has lapsed
          (e.g. after a shattered runestone sent us off to make a new one). It now
          relinks and retries once before concluding the scroll is locked. Also stopped
          sending "get #" with a blank id when restoring hands after making a rune.
        - Fixed a shattered ag'loenar runestone going undetected: the game sometimes puts
          the shatter and "The scroll glows dimly for a moment." in one line, and the
          glow check (added in 1.4) matched first. Shatter is now checked first, and
          "lose your focus" (no runestone in hand) also fetches a new one.
        - Fixed unlocking not stopping on "The runestone is momentarily surrounded by a
          bright white aura" (scroll can't be unlocked further): the stop check only
          knew the "dim" wording and now matches "white aura". Also waits for the scroll
          to be back in hand after fetching a rune, instead of waving at a blank hand.
        - Added --cont=<container> (e.g. ;infuse --cont=kit): stows the finished scroll
          there instead of scrollsack/vibrantscrollsack, for scrolls meant for other
          characters.
        - Added --spells=101,103: unlock only until those spells are unlocked (waving
          quiss'fyn and checking with odeir'cos in between), then infuse, ignoring the
          other spells on the scroll.
        - Opens closed containers as needed (infusesack, scrollsack, vibrantscrollsack,
          --cont) and closes only the ones it opened when it finishes, so a closed
          scrollsack no longer breaks stowing the finished scroll.
        - Encumbrance check up front: at infuse_max_encumbrance percent (default 25) or more
          with silvers on hand, runs to the bank, deposits everything and returns first, so
          too many silvers can't stop the runestone purchase (;vars set
          infuse_max_encumbrance=0 turns it off).
        - Cheaper runestones: buys a smooth stone from the general store's backroom and an
          aish'vrak potion from the alchemist and pours one on the other, instead of the
          10k premade runestone (about 6k). Falls back to the premade one when the stone
          or potion isn't for sale (no backroom access); infuse_smooth_stone=false skips
          the general store stop. Hands are also cleared before the bank run now.
        - Stops itself if you die. A waved stone once exploded a scroll and killed the
          character, and the script kept going (rummaging, waving, buying) while dead.

=end

# Globals
$scroll_id = -1

# Container override from --cont=<container>: where finished scrolls go instead
# of scrollsack/vibrantscrollsack (nil = use the sacks).
$cont_override = nil

# Spell numbers from --spells=101,103: unlock only until these are unlocked
# (nil = unlock everything).
$target_spells = nil

# Containers this script opened (so it can close them again when it's done) and
# ones it has already looked at, by lowercase name.
$opened_containers = []
$checked_containers = []

# Encumbrance percent at or above which we dump our silvers in the bank before
# starting. Too many coins on hand can stop you buying a runestone partway
# through making a rune. ;vars set infuse_max_encumbrance=<percent>; 0 = off.
def max_encumbrance
	v = UserVars.infuse_max_encumbrance.to_s.strip
	v =~ /\A\d+\z/ ? v.to_i : 25
end

# If we're encumbered and carrying silvers, run to the bank, deposit them all
# and come back, so a heavy coin purse can't kill the run mid-purchase.
def deposit_if_encumbered
	limit = max_encumbrance
	return if limit.zero?
	enc = Char.percent_encumbrance
	return if enc < limit

	silver = (Lich::Util.silver_count rescue 0).to_i
	if silver <= 0
		echo "Encumbrance is #{enc}% but there are no silvers on hand to deposit - carrying on."
		return
	end

	echo "Encumbrance #{enc}% with #{silver} silvers on hand - depositing them first."
	start = Room.current.id
	start_script('go2',['bank'])
	wait_while {running?('go2')}
	fput "deposit all"
	sleep 1
	start_script('go2',[start])
	wait_while {running?('go2')}
	echo "Encumbrance now #{Char.percent_encumbrance}%."
end

# Open a container if it's closed, remembering that we did so it gets closed
# again when the script ends. Containers that were already open are left alone.
def open_container(name)
	name = name.to_s.strip
	return if name.empty? || $checked_containers.include?(name.downcase)
	$checked_containers << name.downcase
	result = dothistimeout "open my #{name}", 5, /^You open|^You carefully|^You unfasten|^That is already open\./
	$opened_containers << name if result =~ /^You (?:open|carefully|unfasten)/
end

# Make blank runestones from a general-store smooth stone + alchemist aish'vrak
# potion instead of buying the premade one? On by default; it needs backroom
# access to the general store (it falls back by itself when the stone isn't for
# sale). ;vars set infuse_smooth_stone=false to skip the extra stop.
def smooth_stone_enabled?
	UserVars.infuse_smooth_stone.to_s !~ /\A(?:false|no|off|0)\z/i
end

# Make the rune_name rune
#
# Preconditions:
# 	- Scroll in right hand
def make_rune (rune_name)
	return_room = Room.current.id
	
	# Free a hand for a purchase without disturbing the rune brush (a blind
	# "stow left" can stow the brush itself, after which every dip/draw fails).
	free_hand = lambda do
		held = [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].compact.find { |o| o.noun !~ /brush/ }
		fput "stow ##{held.id}" if held
	end

	order = lambda do |item_name|
		echo "#{item_name}"
		orderlist = dothis "order", /#{item_name}/
		orderlist = orderlist.split('   ')
		orderlist = orderlist.each.find{|item| item.include? "#{item_name}"}
		ordernum = orderlist.scan(/\d+/).first
		fput "order #{ordernum}"
		buy_result = dothistimeout "buy", 5, /Sold for|need a free hand/
		3.times do
			break unless buy_result =~ /need a free hand/
			free_hand.call
			sleep 0.5
			buy_result = dothistimeout "buy", 5, /Sold for|need a free hand/
		end
		buy_result
	end
	
	# Both hands are needed (brush + cup/ink, or stone + potion), so clear
	# anything held first - otherwise "get cup" fails with "You need a free hand"
	# and the brush ends up stowed by mistake. Remember what was held so it can be
	# picked back up when we're done.
	original_hands = [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].compact.map { |o| o.id.to_s }.select { |id| id =~ /\A\d+\z/ }
	if !original_hands.empty?
		fput "stow all"
		sleep 1
	end

	# The first item in either hand (matching /match/ by noun if given), once the
	# game has caught up - GameObj lags what the game just handed us.
	hand_item = lambda do |match = nil, timeout = 5|
		end_time = Time.now.to_f + timeout
		item = nil
		loop do
			item = [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].compact.find { |o| o.id.to_s =~ /\A\d+\z/ && (match.nil? || o.noun =~ match) }
			break if item || Time.now.to_f > end_time
			sleep 0.1
		end
		item
	end

	# Does this shop's catalog list something matching pattern? Looks without
	# ordering, so a shop that doesn't stock it (or a general store whose backroom
	# we can't enter) can't leave "order" waiting forever for a line that never comes.
	shop_sells = lambda do |pattern|
		collect_lines("order", /You can APPRAISE, INSPECT or DESCRIBE/, 8).any? { |l| l =~ pattern }
	end

	# Withdraw money
	start_script('go2',['bank'])
	wait_while {running?('go2')}
	# 1 second isn't enough for the teller's response to reliably land in time,
	# which caused this to report "not enough money" even after a successful
	# withdrawal.
	have_money = dothistimeout "withdraw 20000 silver", 5, /20,000 silvers/
	if !have_money
		echo "You don't have enough money for runestones! You need at least 20,000 silvers in your bank account."
		exit
	end

	# Cheaper blank runestone: a "smooth stone" from the general store's backroom plus
	# an aish'vrak potion from the alchemist, poured together, make the same blank
	# runestone the alchemist sells premade (about 6k instead of 10k). The stone is
	# bought first and stowed; stone_id stays nil if any of it isn't available, and we
	# fall back to buying the premade runestone.
	stone_id = nil
	if smooth_stone_enabled?
		start_script('go2',['general store'])
		wait_while {running?('go2')}
		if shop_sells.call(/smooth stone/)
			order.("smooth stone")
			stone = hand_item.call(/stone/)
			if stone
				stone_id = stone.id
				fput "stow ##{stone_id}"
				sleep 1
			end
		else
			echo "No smooth stone for sale here (no backroom access?) - buying the premade runestone instead."
		end
	end

	# It's just easier to withdraw money and go to the alchemist for this step
	start_script('go2',['alchemist'])
	wait_while {running?('go2')}

	if stone_id
		if shop_sells.call(/aish'vrak/)
			fput "get ##{stone_id}"
			if hand_item.call(/stone/)
				order.("aish'vrak")
				poured = collect_lines("pour potion on stone", /shatters into twinkling dust|What were you referring to|Pour what/, 8)
				if poured.any? { |l| l =~ /shatters into twinkling dust/ }
					sleep 1
					blank = hand_item.call(/stone/)          # pouring can swap the item's id
					stone_id = blank ? blank.id : nil
				else
					echo "Pouring the potion didn't work - buying the premade runestone instead."
					stone_id = nil
				end
			else
				stone_id = nil
			end
			fput "stow ##{stone_id}" if stone_id
			fput "stow all" unless stone_id        # a leftover potion/stone from a failed attempt
			sleep 1
		else
			echo "No aish'vrak potion for sale here - buying the premade runestone instead."
			stone_id = nil
		end
	end

	fput "get my brush in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
	brush_state = dothistimeout "look at my brush", 5, /covered in|clean|dried|dry/
	echo "#{brush_state}"
	
	# Clean brush
	if brush_state =~ /dried|dry/
		find_cup = dothistimeout "get cup in my #{UserVars.infusesack}", 5, /You remove|You get|You grab/
		order.("cup") if !find_cup
		fput "dip brush in my cup"
		# Sorena's (Icemule) spoils the cup's water after one rinse and sets the
		# cup aside, so this put harmlessly fails there; other towns reuse it.
		fput "put cup in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
	end

	# Dip ink
	if brush_state =~ /clean|dried|dry/
		got_ink = dothistimeout "get ink in my #{UserVars.infusesack}", 5, /You remove|You get|You grab/
		got_ink ||= dothistimeout "get bottle in my #{UserVars.infusesack}", 5, /You remove|You get|You grab/
		order.("ink") unless got_ink
		# The ink item's noun varies by town: most sell "a bottle of rune ink"
		# (answers to "ink"), but Sorena's in Icemule sells "a ... ink bottle"
		# whose noun is "bottle". Read the real noun off the item in hand rather
		# than assuming, or the dip silently no-ops and the draw fails.
		ink = [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].compact.find { |o| o.noun =~ /ink|bottle/ }
		ink_noun = ink ? ink.noun : "ink"
		fput "dip brush in my #{ink_noun}"
		fput "put #{ink_noun} in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
	end
	
	# Get the blank stone: the one we made, or the alchemist's premade runestone
	blank_noun = "runestone"
	if stone_id
		fput "get ##{stone_id}"
		blank_noun = "stone"
	else
		order.("runestone")
	end

	# Draw rune
	draw = dothistimeout "draw #{rune_name} rune on #{blank_noun}", 5, /cleaned off first|will need ink|Roundtime/
	if !draw.include? 'Roundtime'
		echo "Something went wrong"
		exit
	end

	waitrt?
	fput "put brush in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
	
	start_script('go2',['bank'])
	wait_while{running?('go2')}
	fput "deposit all"
	start_script('go2',[return_room])
	wait_while{running?('go2')}

	original_hands.each { |id| fput "get ##{id}" }
end	

# Find the rune_name rune in your infusesack, or make it.
#
# Preconditions:
#	- Scroll in right hand
def find_rune(rune_name)
	find_rune = dothis "rummage in my #{UserVars.infusesack} runestone #{rune_name}", /drawn on it|can't seem to locate/
	if find_rune.include? "can't seem to locate"
		fput "put right in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
		fput "stow all"
		make_rune(rune_name)
		fput "get ##{$scroll_id}"
		return true
	elsif find_rune.include? "drawn on it"
		return true
	else
		return false
	end
end

# Send action and collect every line of the response up to (and including) a
# line matching terminator.
#
# dothistimeout only returns the single line that matched the terminator,
# which loses the rest of a multi-line block - like the full list of spells
# shown by "wave left at scroll", where a wave can produce both the "altered"
# success line and a "disintegrates" line in the same response and we need to
# see both, not just whichever comes first.
def collect_lines(action, terminator, timeout = 5)
	end_time = Time.now.to_f + timeout
	lines = []
	Script.current.clear
	fput action
	loop do
		line = get?
		if line
			lines << line
			break if line =~ terminator
		else
			sleep 0.1
		end
		break if Time.now.to_f > end_time
	end
	lines
end

# Count how many spells on the scroll in your right hand are still locked.
#
# The odeir'cos charge listing shows "...and the potential to add X charges"
# for spells that are already unlocked; a locked spell's line doesn't have
# that clause, so its absence is what marks a spell as still needing quiss'fyn.
#
# Preconditions:
#	- Scroll in right hand
def count_locked_spells
	read_spell_status.values.count(false)
end

# Read the scroll in your right hand with the odeir'cos rune and return
# { spell number => unlocked? } for every spell on it (see count_locked_spells
# for how locked vs unlocked is told apart). Leaves the rune stowed again.
#
# Preconditions:
#	- Scroll in right hand, left hand free
def read_spell_status
	find_rune("odeir'cos")
	lines = collect_lines("wave left at my #{GameObj.right_hand}", /Roundtime/, 5)
	fput "put left in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
	status = {}
	lines.each do |line|
		m = line.match(/^\s*\((\d+)\)/)
		status[m[1].to_i] = !!(line =~ /potential to add/) if m
	end
	status
end

# Is this wave response the game saying nothing more can be unlocked?
# There are several flavor-text variants ("shakes slightly"/"violently, but
# nothing happens", "surrounded by a dim/bright white aura", ...), so match
# loosely - another variant we haven't seen yet could turn up the same way
# "bright white aura" did. The aura means the scroll can't be unlocked any
# further, whatever the odeir'cos count says.
def nothing_left_to_unlock?(wave_lines)
	wave_lines.any? { |line| line =~ /but nothing happens|white aura/ }
end

# find_rune can put the scroll back in hand with "get", and GameObj lags the
# game briefly - waving then interpolated an empty hand object into the
# command ("wave left at my #<Lich::Common::GameObj...>"). Wait until the
# right hand has a real item again.
def wait_for_right_hand(timeout = 5)
	end_time = Time.now.to_f + timeout
	until (hand = GameObj.right_hand) && hand.noun.to_s != ''
		break if Time.now.to_f > end_time
		sleep 0.1
	end
end

# Unlock the locked spells on the scroll in your right hand.
#
# Checks with odeir'cos first to see how many spells still need unlocking,
# then waves quiss'fyn exactly that many times instead of waving blindly
# until the scroll reports fully charged.
#
# Preconditions:
#	- Scroll in right hand
def unlock_spells
	return unlock_target_spells($target_spells) if $target_spells

	locked = count_locked_spells
	if locked.zero?
		echo "No locked spells found."
		return
	end
	echo "#{locked} locked spell(s) found, unlocking..."

	find_rune("quiss'fyn")
	wait_for_right_hand
	while locked > 0
		wave_lines = collect_lines("wave left at my #{GameObj.right_hand}", /Roundtime/, 5)
		waitrt?
		waitcastrt?
		# Safety net: the game itself says nothing's left to unlock, so stop
		# regardless of what our count says, rather than risk waving forever
		# on a stale rune if the count is ever off.
		if nothing_left_to_unlock?(wave_lines)
			echo "Scroll reports no more locked spells."
			break
		end
		if wave_lines.any? { |line| line =~ /disintegrates/ }
			find_rune("quiss'fyn")
			wait_for_right_hand
		end
		locked -= 1 if wave_lines.any? { |line| line =~ /has somehow been altered/ }
	end
	echo "Scroll fully unlocked."
	fput "put left in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
end

# Unlock only until the given spells (an array of spell numbers) are unlocked.
#
# quiss'fyn unlocks a random locked spell per wave and only unlocked spells get
# infused, so this waves, checks with odeir'cos, and repeats until every
# target is unlocked - ignoring whatever else on the scroll happens to unlock
# along the way. Each pass needs at least one "altered" wave per target still
# locked, so it only re-checks after that many (saves swapping runes for a
# check that can't have finished yet).
#
# Stops without wasting charges if a target isn't on the scroll at all, and
# exits if the scroll can't be unlocked any further with targets still locked.
#
# Preconditions:
#	- Scroll in right hand
def unlock_target_spells(targets)
	status = read_spell_status
	if status.empty?
		status = read_spell_status
		if status.empty?
			echo "Couldn't read the spells on this scroll."
			exit
		end
	end

	missing = targets.reject { |n| status.key?(n) }
	unless missing.empty?
		echo "Spell(s) #{missing.join(', ')} aren't on this scroll (it has #{status.keys.join(', ')}) - not wasting any runestone charges."
		exit
	end

	pending = targets.reject { |n| status[n] }
	if pending.empty?
		echo "Spell(s) #{targets.join(', ')} already unlocked."
		return
	end
	echo "Unlocking until #{targets.join(', ')} are unlocked (still locked: #{pending.join(', ')})..."

	find_rune("quiss'fyn")
	wait_for_right_hand
	until pending.empty?
		gained = 0
		stuck = false
		while gained < pending.size
			wave_lines = collect_lines("wave left at my #{GameObj.right_hand}", /Roundtime/, 5)
			waitrt?
			waitcastrt?
			if nothing_left_to_unlock?(wave_lines)
				stuck = true
				break
			end
			if wave_lines.any? { |line| line =~ /disintegrates/ }
				find_rune("quiss'fyn")
				wait_for_right_hand
			end
			gained += 1 if wave_lines.any? { |line| line =~ /has somehow been altered/ }
		end

		fput "put left in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
		status = read_spell_status
		pending = targets.reject { |n| status[n] }
		if pending.empty?
			echo "Spell(s) #{targets.join(', ')} unlocked."
			return
		end
		if stuck
			echo "The scroll can't be unlocked any further, but spell(s) #{pending.join(', ')} are still locked - stopping."
			exit
		end
		echo "Still locked: #{pending.join(', ')}"
		find_rune("quiss'fyn")
		wait_for_right_hand
	end
end

# Cast the link (Scroll Infusion, 714) spell on the scroll in your right hand.
#
# Waits for enough mana first so Spell#cast's own energy check can't silently
# no-op the cast (it just echoes 'cast: not enough mana' and returns false).
#
# Returns true if the link was made, or false if you're too injured to cast it.
def link_scroll(infusescroll)
	wait_until { mana >= Spell[714].mana_cost }
	link_result = Spell[714].cast(infusescroll)
	if link_result.to_s.include? "You can't make that dextrous of a move!"
		echo "You are too injured to link to the scroll!"
		return false
	elsif link_result == false
		echo "Failed to link to the scroll!"
		return false
	end
	waitcastrt?
	true
end

# Wait for mana to regen, watching for the link to the scroll slipping in the meantime.
#
# The "You feel your link to the ... slip." message can arrive asynchronously
# at any point (e.g. during waitcastrt?, before this is even called), and
# dothistimeout's Script.current.clear would otherwise silently discard it
# before the next infuse attempt ever sees it. So every iteration - even if
# mana is already high enough to return immediately - must drain and check
# whatever's currently buffered before deciding we're done waiting.
#
# Returns true once mana regens, or false if the link slipped and we couldn't relink.
def wait_for_mana(infusescroll, threshold = 20)
	loop do
		while (line = get?)
			if line =~ /You feel your link to the .* slip\./
				echo "Lost the link to the scroll, relinking..."
				return false unless link_scroll(infusescroll)
			end
		end
		return true if mana > threshold
		sleep 0.1
	end
end

# Whether to pause for a "nod" when an infusion is a struggle. On by default;
# turn off with ;vars set infuse_safe=false to just keep trying.
def infuse_safe?
	UserVars.infuse_safe.to_s !~ /\A(?:false|no|off|0)\z/i
end

# Fully infuse all unlocked spells on the scroll in your right hand
def infuse
	find_rune("ag'loenar")
	infusescroll = "#" + GameObj.right_hand.id
	exit unless link_scroll(infusescroll)
	relinked = false

	loop do
		break unless wait_for_mana(infusescroll)
		# The terminator regex must include every phrase an elsif below checks
		# for - dothistimeout only returns a line once it matches this regex,
		# so a phrase missing here (like the rune shattering) just times out
		# to nil instead of ever reaching its handling branch.
		infuse_line = dothistimeout "infuse my #{GameObj.right_hand}", 5, /glows dimly for a moment|mana dissipates|You are not prepared to infuse that|cracks slightly and then shatters|You strain to harness|lose your focus/
		waitcastrt?

		# The shatter check has to come first: the game can report the shatter and
		# "The scroll glows dimly for a moment." in the same line, and the glow
		# check would swallow it, leaving us infusing with a rune that's gone.
		if infuse_line.include? 'cracks slightly and then shatters'
			find_rune("ag'loenar")
		elsif infuse_line.include? 'lose your focus'
			# No runestone in hand to channel through. Only fetch one if the left hand
			# really isn't holding a runestone (find_rune would stall on a full hand).
			left = GameObj.left_hand
			find_rune("ag'loenar") unless left && left.noun =~ /runestone|stone/
		elsif infuse_line.include? 'glows dimly for a moment'
			relinked = false
		elsif infuse_line.include? 'grows cold'
			echo "Scroll locked!!"
			break
		elsif infuse_line.include? 'not prepared to infuse'
			# "Not prepared" means the scroll is locked OR we've lost our link to it
			# (e.g. after the runestone shattered and a new one had to be made, which
			# takes long enough for the link to lapse). Relink once and retry before
			# concluding it's locked.
			if relinked
				echo "Scroll locked!!"
				break
			end
			echo "Not prepared to infuse - relinking before calling it locked..."
			break unless link_scroll(infusescroll)
			relinked = true
		elsif infuse_line.include? 'mana dissipates'
			echo "Scroll fully infused!"
			break
		elsif infuse_line.include? 'You strain to harness'
			if infuse_safe?
				echo "You appear to be struggling with infusing this scroll, if you want to continue nod within the next 10 seconds"
				continue = matchtimeout 10, "You nod"
				break if !continue
			end
		end
	end
end

# Checks spells are unlocked and how charged they are, then stows the scroll
# in scrollsack - or vibrantscrollsack if it's a vibrant ink scroll.
#
# The odeir'cos charge listing shows "X charges remaining" for a regular
# scroll's spells, but "X time remaining" (temporary knowledge, no charges)
# for a vibrant one - so the wave response alone is enough to tell them apart.
def check_charge
	fput "put left in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
	find_rune("odeir'cos")
	charge_line = dothistimeout "wave left at my #{GameObj.right_hand}", 5, /time remaining|charges remaining/
	is_vibrant = charge_line =~ /time remaining/ ? true : false

	if $cont_override
		echo "Storing in #{$cont_override} (--cont override)."
		open_container($cont_override)
		fput "put right in my #{$cont_override}"
	elsif is_vibrant && UserVars.vibrantscrollsack && UserVars.vibrantscrollsack.length >= 3
		echo "Vibrant scroll detected, storing in vibrantscrollsack."
		open_container(UserVars.vibrantscrollsack)
		fput "put right in my #{UserVars.vibrantscrollsack}"
	else
		echo "Vibrant scroll detected but no vibrantscrollsack is set (;vars set vibrantscrollsack=<container name>) - storing in scrollsack instead." if is_vibrant
		open_container(UserVars.scrollsack)
		fput "put right in my #{UserVars.scrollsack}"
	end
end

# Check that you're holding a scroll in your right hand & set scroll_id
def check_for_scroll
	if !GameObj.right_hand || !(GameObj.right_hand.noun =~ /scroll|parchment|palimpsest|paper|papyrus|vellum/)
		echo "No scroll to unlock/infuse/check!  Make sure you have a scroll in your right hand."
		exit
	end
	$scroll_id = GameObj.right_hand.id
end


# Validate arguments
if UserVars.infusesack
	if UserVars.infusesack.length < 3
		echo "You must define an infusesack - ;vars set infusesack = <container name>"
		exit
	end
else	
	echo "You must define an infusesack - ;vars set infusesack = <container name>"
	exit
end

if UserVars.scrollsack
	if UserVars.scrollsack.length < 3
		echo "You must define a scrollsack - ;vars set scrollsack = <container name>"
		exit
	end
else	
	echo "You must define a scrollsack - ;vars set scrollsack = <container name>"
	exit
end

# Pull --cont=<container> out of the arguments; what's left is the command.
args = Script.current.vars[1..-1] || []
cont_arg = args.find { |a| a =~ /\A--cont=/i }
if cont_arg
	args.delete(cont_arg)
	$cont_override = cont_arg.sub(/\A--cont=/i, '').gsub(/\A["']|["']\z/, '').strip
	if $cont_override.empty?
		echo "--cont needs a container, e.g. ;infuse --cont=kit"
		exit
	end
end

spells_arg = args.find { |a| a =~ /\A--spells=/i }
if spells_arg
	args.delete(spells_arg)
	list = spells_arg.sub(/\A--spells=/i, '').gsub(/\A["']|["']\z/, '').strip
	if list !~ /\A\d+(?:\s*,\s*\d+)*\z/
		echo "--spells needs a comma-separated list of spell numbers, e.g. ;infuse --spells=101,103"
		exit
	end
	$target_spells = list.split(',').map { |n| n.strip.to_i }.uniq
end

# Open the infusesack up front (the runestone gear lives there), and put
# whatever we opened back to closed when the script ends - however it ends.
# scrollsack/vibrantscrollsack/--cont are opened when a scroll is stowed in them.
if args[0] != 'help'
	before_dying {
		# Nothing to close once you're dead (the game just refuses everything).
		$opened_containers.each { |c| fput "close my #{c}" } unless dead?
	}

	# A scroll can kill you outright (waving a quiss'fyn stone over a scroll once made it
	# explode: "Fire burns through neck and destroys carotid artery", then "It seems you
	# have died, my friend"). The script used to carry on regardless - rummaging, waving
	# and buying with a dead character - so stop it the moment the game says you're dead.
	my_name = Script.current.name
	Thread.new do
		loop do
			sleep 0.5
			next unless dead?
			echo "You have died - stopping #{my_name}."
			Script.kill(my_name)
			break
		end
	end
	open_container(UserVars.infusesack)
	deposit_if_encumbered unless args[0] == 'check'
end

# Main
if args.empty?
	check_for_scroll
	unlock_spells
	infuse
	check_charge

elsif args[0] == 'unlock'
	check_for_scroll
	unlock_spells

elsif args[0] == 'infuse'
	check_for_scroll
	infuse
	check_charge

elsif args[0] == 'rune'
	make_rune(args[1])

elsif args[0] == 'check'
	check_for_scroll
	check_charge

elsif args[0] == 'help'
	respond "First, set your <infusesack> and <scrollsack> (can be the same):"
	respond "    ;vars set infusesack=<container name>"
    respond "    ;vars set scrollsack=<container name>"
	respond ""
	respond "Optionally, set a <vibrantscrollsack> to keep vibrant-ink scrolls separate:"
	respond "    ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=<container name>"
	respond ""
	respond "    infusesack        - runestones and runestone-making tools (brush, ink, cup)"
	respond "    scrollsack        - finished scrolls"
	respond "    vibrantscrollsack - finished scrolls whose spell descriptions come back \"vibrant\";"
	respond "                        falls back to scrollsack if this isn't set"
	respond ""
	respond "CURRENT SETTINGS:"
	respond "    infusesack:        #{UserVars.infusesack || '(not set)'}"
	respond "    scrollsack:        #{UserVars.scrollsack || '(not set)'}"
	respond "    vibrantscrollsack: #{UserVars.vibrantscrollsack || '(not set)'}"
	respond "    infuse_smooth_stone: #{smooth_stone_enabled?} (make runestones from a general-store smooth stone + aish'vrak potion; false = buy premade)"
	respond "    infuse_max_encumbrance: #{max_encumbrance} (deposit silvers at the bank first at or above this %; 0 = off)"
	respond "    infuse_safe:       #{infuse_safe?} (;vars set infuse_safe=false to never pause for a nod)"
	respond ""
	respond "You need at least 20,000 silvers in your local bank - whenever a rune needs"
	respond "to be made (;infuse rune, or automatically during unlock/infuse), it withdraws"
	respond "a flat 20,000 to cover runestones, ink, a cup, etc."
	respond ""
	respond "USAGE:"
	respond "    ;infuse [unlock|infuse|check|rune <rune name>] [--cont=<container>] [--spells=<n,n>]"
	respond ""
	respond "    ;infuse                    - Unlock & infuse scroll in your right hand (unlocks every"
	respond "                                 locked spell unless --spells is given)"
	respond "    ;infuse unlock             - Unlock the scroll in your right hand (all locked spells,"
	respond "                                 or just the --spells ones)"
	respond "    ;infuse infuse             - Infuse scroll in your right hand"
	respond "    ;infuse rune <rune name>   - Make a runestone with rune <rune name>"
    respond "    ;infuse check              - Check for charges of a scroll in your right hand"
	respond ""
	respond "    --cont=<container>         - Put the finished scroll in <container> instead of"
	respond "                                 scrollsack/vibrantscrollsack, e.g. ;infuse --cont=kit"
	respond "                                 (for scrolls you're passing to another character)"
	respond "    --spells=101,103           - Unlock only until these spells are unlocked (checking"
	respond "                                 with odeir'cos between waves), then infuse; ignores the"
	respond "                                 rest of the scroll. Exits without waving if a listed"
	respond "                                 spell isn't on the scroll."
	respond ""
	exit
end

#cleanup (in case you still have a runestone in your hand)
fput "put left in my #{UserVars.infusesack}"
